# themselves (see ask-self's ASK_SELF_INTEGRATION.md) rather than inheriting it here.
/ask_self/
/scripts/ask-self-ingest.sh
/scripts/ask-self-query.sh
/.claude/commands/reingest.md
/.claude/commands/ask_self.md
# Local working index lives under temp/rag/ (already ignored via /temp/); these lines
# also catch the per-DB sidecars anywhere they land.
temp/rag/
temp/ask-self-rag.env
*__embed_cache.sqlite
*__events.jsonl
# ask-self generated architecture doc (falls back to ASK_SELF.md; our ARCHITECTURE.md is hand-owned).
ASK_SELF.md
ARCHITECTURE-BAK.md

# Sentinel Tier 1 debug capture — local only, never committed.
debug.log
/BTW

# Marathon per-phase run artifacts (GH-461 follow-up). marathon-drive writes phases/<phase-id>/
# {RELAY.md,ESCALATION.md} into the TARGET ROOT, which for a same-repo run is this repo. They are run
# output, not source: a dry run alone rewrites them, and the diff is machine-dependent because they
# embed absolute paths — so they churn for whoever runs the suite and revert for whoever last
# committed them (#401/#461, observed live three times over 2026-08-05/06).
#
# Root-anchored on purpose: a fixture's own phases/ under some subdirectory is a test's business, and
# every test that reads one does so through its own $ROOT, never this path.
#
# NOTE this does NOT untrack the ~72 already-committed records under phases/<run-specific-name>/.
# Those carry unique per-run directory names, so they do not churn — they are marathon history and
# stay tracked deliberately. The one exception, phases/p1/, is untracked in the same commit as this
# rule: `p1` is a GENERIC id that every run and several tests reuse, so each one overwrote the last.
/phases/
